    <table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="grid" style="margin: 0;">
                <tr id="comment-header-6626105"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="61099c519798100070a55d79"
                id="word_commented_61099c519798100070a55d79"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=61099c519798100070a55d79">
                    Karen Levine-Flandrup
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">22/Jan/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6626105"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Aa202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" class="user-hover" rel="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" data-account-id="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" accountid="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762" rel="noreferrer">Hina Khan</a> this process was transitioned to my team in early January.  We do not see approvals for this to go to production.  Do you have an approval message from Mike Catania that you can share?  Otherwise you are in the backlog of the process and does not currently have approvals to go to production on requested date of april.</p>

<p>Please advise.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-6629762"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762"
                id="word_commented_557058:a202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Aa202c244-8bed-40ab-a122-b4c52da1c762">
                    Hina Khan
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">22/Jan/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6629762"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Thank you, <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=61099c519798100070a55d79" class="user-hover" rel="61099c519798100070a55d79" data-account-id="61099c519798100070a55d79" accountid="61099c519798100070a55d79" rel="noreferrer">Karen Levine-Flandrup</a> , for the update. We do not have any approval yet, and April is the date the business is considering at the moment. We have involved <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60677cff1613f3006825fa65" class="user-hover" rel="60677cff1613f3006825fa65" data-account-id="60677cff1613f3006825fa65" accountid="60677cff1613f3006825fa65" rel="noreferrer">Ian Lopez</a>  and his team and completed a review. Next, we have a follow-up regarding the EA decision. </p>

<p>During our last call, we learned about the IT Sterllus process for AI approval, so we would like to begin that process with your team. If April is not feasible, could you please let me know the process and any follow-ups required with you and your team so we can outline and define our processes? Thank you.</p>

<p>CC: <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3Ab4a6be5b-b4cf-4315-ba1a-72c750c9171d" class="user-hover" rel="712020:b4a6be5b-b4cf-4315-ba1a-72c750c9171d" data-account-id="712020:b4a6be5b-b4cf-4315-ba1a-72c750c9171d" accountid="712020:b4a6be5b-b4cf-4315-ba1a-72c750c9171d" rel="noreferrer">Brian Dees</a> , <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60677739b30f0d0070562bcd" class="user-hover" rel="60677739b30f0d0070562bcd" data-account-id="60677739b30f0d0070562bcd" accountid="60677739b30f0d0070562bcd" rel="noreferrer">Vidya Rai</a> , <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617ddda1f6da6a006a49c084" class="user-hover" rel="617ddda1f6da6a006a49c084" data-account-id="617ddda1f6da6a006a49c084" accountid="617ddda1f6da6a006a49c084" rel="noreferrer">Rajeev Haswani</a> </p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-6645349"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="60677bf995acf80071c01bc2"
                id="word_commented_60677bf995acf80071c01bc2"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=60677bf995acf80071c01bc2">
                    Chendra Sekhar Grandhi
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">28/Jan/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6645349"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>EA has assessed the capabilities of Pega Voice AI and find it appropriate to be used as ‘Agent Assist’ to BSC customer service team using Pega Shield Advisor today. EA recommends the pilot as BSC already uses Pega Shield Advisor and Pega Voice AI is an addon in the platform to help pre-fill forms/feedback with on Pega Shield Advisor. EA approves to go ahead with the Pega Voice AI pilot.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-6664407"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="61099c519798100070a55d79"
                id="word_commented_61099c519798100070a55d79"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=61099c519798100070a55d79">
                    Karen Levine-Flandrup
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">03/Feb/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6664407"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p><a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=6067773800b79f0070f1cae8" class="user-hover" rel="6067773800b79f0070f1cae8" data-account-id="6067773800b79f0070f1cae8" accountid="6067773800b79f0070f1cae8" rel="noreferrer">Aman Sharma</a> see below for EA approval?  Please update your subtask.</p>


<p> <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=61830cc0f6da6a006a872f9a" class="user-hover" rel="61830cc0f6da6a006a872f9a" data-account-id="61830cc0f6da6a006a872f9a" accountid="61830cc0f6da6a006a872f9a" rel="noreferrer">Michelle Minnick</a> <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A73331039-9d56-4d90-8955-dd58aacf4022" class="user-hover" rel="712020:73331039-9d56-4d90-8955-dd58aacf4022" data-account-id="712020:73331039-9d56-4d90-8955-dd58aacf4022" accountid="712020:73331039-9d56-4d90-8955-dd58aacf4022" rel="noreferrer">Dawn Kinneer</a> looks complete enough to kick off.  Thanks.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-6674530"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
            <a class="user-hover" rel="617dddd3e79ff6006fe8492d"
                id="word_commented_617dddd3e79ff6006fe8492d"
                href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=617dddd3e79ff6006fe8492d">
                    Joe Martinez
                </a>

                                        <font size="-2">
            [
                <font color="#336699">06/Feb/26</font>

                            ]
            </font>

        </td></tr>
        <tr id="comment-body-6674530"><td bgcolor="#ffffff">
            <p>Risk = Medium, per attached assessment. Per question support available, <a href="https://blueshieldca.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/ISRM/pages/1917255764/AI+Use+Case+Risk+Assessment+Process+Support+Guide" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">AI Use Case Risk Assessment – Process Support Guide - Information Security &amp; Risk Management - Confluence</a>. Please let me know if you have any questions.</p>

<p><b>Overall Summary:</b><br/>
The AI Use Case Risk Questionnaire identifies this Voice AI implementation as <b>Medium risk</b>, driven primarily by the presence of PHI, reliance on vendor cloud‑based processing, and the early‑stage maturity of operational controls. The use case remains assistive—not decision‑making—and includes human review of all summaries, reducing safety and fairness risk areas while still requiring appropriate safeguards.</p>

<p><b>Recommended Mitigations:</b><br/>
To manage a Medium‑risk profile, the team should focus on strengthening documentation, enhancing monitoring and drift/bias checks, and ensuring formal security validation prior to scaling beyond pilot. Additional emphasis should be placed on hardening vendor integrations, confirming HIPAA‑aligned safeguards, and maturing operational oversight so the solution can safely progress from pilot to wider deployment.</p>
        </td></tr>
                <tr id="comment-header-6680049"><td bgcolor="#f0f0f0">
            Comment by  
                                                    
                
        
